# A tag may have any name, `pass` and `self` included: whether the action
# function reads its parameters is decided from the actions themselves, not
# from the text they were written as. `prog! = A → (pass)` reads no element,
# so the parser discards the `pass` parameter (or it would not compile).

@lexer
tokens
    a
    eof
    err
'a'                                         → a
.                                           → err

@parser

prog! = A                                   → (pass)
